From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:13:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Anime4K per layer: 2D art textures upscaled one by one,
 cached on disk

With Anime4K above 640x448, every 8/16/32-bit texture of 32x32 or more first seen in a 2D scene is queued (ga2_layers, gs_texpacks.cpp); the presentation runs the filter's network on a few per frame (two 2x chains for 4x, colour bled into transparent pixels, alpha scaled on its own) and hands the result back; the GS's cached textures are dropped now and then so the upscaled ones replace them. Results are kept in <cache>/anime4k. The composed picture is then only scaled (GA2_LAYER_UPSCALE=0: the old pass over the composed picture).
